# lf113, the door-watching vat hand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf113
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_cw_fern_mistshore
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the door-watching vat hand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_the_entry_in_sight_at_supper
likes smoked_eel digging full_larder summer_evenings
dislikes deep_mud waiting
fears a_vat_spoiled_by_dirty_water a_cart_stuck_far_from_home
hopes a_full_larder_for_every_house a_shorter_road_to_the_city
topics work +0.5 home +0.3 travel +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=blunt refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the #vat#, watches the #door# even at supper, and counts every mile of the #cart# road.

words
oath! = By the clean sheet | Vat and water
saying! = Give the pulp time to settle | A clear door makes an easy seat
vat = vat | paper vat
pulp = pulp | wet pulp
sheet = sheet | new sheet
sheets = sheets | drying sheets
paper = paper | rough paper
press = press | printing press
rag = rag | clean rag
rags = rags | sorted rags
water = water | fresh water
bucket = bucket | full bucket
frame = frame | wooden frame
mould = mould | paper mould
felt = felt | damp felt
stack = stack | paper stack
stacks = stacks | paper stacks
ink = ink | black ink
letter = letter | printed letter
letters = letters | printed letters
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | vat work
boss = boss | press owner
cart = cart | goods cart
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
road = road | long road
mile = mile | slow mile
miles = miles | many miles
city = city | distant city
market = market | city market
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | thin coin
bread = bread | oven bread
larder = larder | full larder
meal = meal | evening meal
eel = eel | smoked eel
plate = plate | plain plate
home = home | shared home
house = house | cottage
room = room | small room
door = door | open door
seat = seat | wooden seat
back = back | chair back
window = window | front window
neighbour = neighbour | nearby neighbour
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
friend = friend | old friend
mud = mud | wheel mud
boot = boot | heavy boot
boots = boots | wet boots
rain = rain | steady rain
weather = weather | shifting weather
limp = limp | old limp
knee = knee | stiff knee
garden = garden | little garden
soil = soil | turned soil
spade = spade | garden spade
summer = summer | warm summer
evening = evening | long evening
night = night | dark night
morning = morning | early morning
hour = hour | working hour
hours = hours | working hours
plates = plates | supper plates
frames = frames | wooden frames
table = table | shared table
gate = gate | town gate
festival = festival | crowded festival
wait = wait | long wait
queue = queue | market queue
wagon = wagon | loaded wagon

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : I have hauled #paper# there and counted every dirty #mile# back. | Their #market# forgets the #hands# that made it.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A #larder# should never stand empty while a #neighbour# has #bread#. | Put a #meal# on the #plate# first.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : There is more noise than supper at a #festival#. | Someone always spills a drink beside the #door#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# rises while my #coin# stays thin. | They weigh our #sheets# and leave out the #hours#.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I can set a #stranger# at the #table# and bring another #plate#. | A hungry traveller can sit where I see the #door#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Another week of #work# buys less #bread#. | My #hands# know the change before any account does.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# brings our #paper# to the #market#. | Its #mud# has taken enough from my #cart#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Keep the #door# in view. | #greet#. I have just lifted a #sheet# from the #vat#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : There is #eel# in the #larder# if you are hungry. | Sit here; I will take the other #seat#.
line @1 greet.return : The last #stack# is still damp to the touch. | Come in before the #rain# reaches the #door#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I saved you a #plate# by the #window#. | Come inside and dry those #boots#.
line @1 again.open : I was telling you about the #cart# on the #road#. | The #vat# took another #bucket#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have #sheets# to turn. | Mind the #mud# beside the #gate#.
line @1 farewell.return : Next time the #paper# may be dry. | Come back when the #evening# is long.
line @1 react.news : Tell it plainly while I put down this #frame#. | Did it happen on the #road#?
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody at the #press# has said a word of it. | Who brought this from the #city#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard the shape of it at the #market#. | Your account fills a gap for me.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would ask who watched the #cart# leave. | Which #hand# was near enough to see it happen?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Sit down; I can put the #work# aside. | That is hard news to carry through the #door#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good; I will find another #plate#. | That calls for the better #bread#.
line @1 answer.how : My #knee# aches, but the #vat# is sound. | Better since the #cart# came home.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am lifting this #frame# straight. | Wait until the #sheet# is on the #felt#.
line @1 ask.how : How did your #boots# fare on that #road#? | Have you eaten today?
line @1 sympathise : Let me bring you a #meal# before you speak. | Sit where the #window# gives you light.
line @1 reassure : We can find a dry way round the #mud#. | There is room at our #table# tonight.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave a full #vat# unattended. | I have promised these #sheets# by #morning#.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand; I will finish the #stack# here. | Then keep your #boots# clear of the #mud#.
line @1 thank : The #frame# stayed level because of your steady grip. | That #bread# helped more than you know.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had filled the #bucket# for my own use. | I was walking past your #door#.
line @1 preclose : The #sheets# need turning before dark. | I should get the #cart# under cover.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You would sit with your #back# to any #door#. | Your #spade# has had a longer rest than I have.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That #sheet# is almost dry. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will try the #road# tomorrow.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #frame# level until the #water# drains. | Eat before setting out with a full #cart#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Take company on the #road# tonight. | Keep the #wagon# near the other travellers.
scene clean_water
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dirty #water# leaves marks in a fresh #sheet#. | I fetch another #bucket# before I waste the #pulp#.
b : Can you see the dirt? | Does it take long?
a : Against the light. | Longer than fetching water.

scene lifted_frame
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I lift the #frame# evenly from the #vat#. | A tilted #mould# sends #pulp# to one corner.
b : What happens then? | Can you fix it?
a : A thin edge tears. | Back into the #vat#.

scene rag_sorting
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Good #rags# make a stronger #sheet# than the scraps in the bottom #bucket#. | I sort before dawn.
b : Who brings the rags? | Do you discard many?
a : Neighbours and traders. | More than I like.

scene wet_felt
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Damp #felt# takes the fresh #paper# without pulling it apart. | I keep a dry piece ready as well.
b : When do you switch? | Is it heavy?
a : When the first sticks. | By the end of the day.

scene drying_stack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The top #sheet# can feel dry while the middle of the #stack# stays wet. | I turn the whole lot.
b : Every day? | What if it rains?
a : Most mornings. | Then I move them inside.

scene printed_letter
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A clean #letter# starts with a sound #sheet#. | I can spot my own rough #paper# under the #ink#.
b : Does the printer know? | Does it matter?
a : Usually. | The #letters# bleed less.

scene paper_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A buyer counts finished #sheets#, not the #hours# beside the #vat#. | I count both.
b : Can you ask for more? | Who sets the price?
a : I do ask. | The #market# has its say.

scene city_cart
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I rode beside a #cart# of #paper# until the #city# gates came into view. | The return #miles# felt longer.
b : Why go yourself? | Did you stay?
a : To keep it dry. | Only until the #wagon# was empty.

scene broken_wheel
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #wheel# stuck in #mud# once cost us half a day. | I dug around it with my bare #hands#.
b : Did it come free? | Who helped?
a : Eventually. | A passing #hand#.

scene door_seat
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take the #seat# facing the #door# without thinking now. | I like to know when a #friend# arrives.
b : Even at home? | Does anyone object?
a : Especially there. | They know my habit.

scene shared_larder
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# has several #hands# and one #larder#. | I can tell by supper whether everyone ate.
b : Do you keep count? | What if it runs low?
a : Of the #plates#. | We share what is there.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# with fresh #bread# is enough after a day at the #vat#. | I keep a little for the road.
b : Do you smoke it? | How long does it last?
a : I buy it ready. | Long enough for a journey.

scene garden_hour
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An #hour# digging in the #garden# loosens what the #press# stiffens. | The #spade# rests against our back wall.
b : What grows there? | Do you rest afterward?
a : What the #soil# will take. | At supper.

scene summer_evening
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long #summer# #evening# lets me finish the #stack# and still see the #garden#. | I use every bit of it.
b : Do you ever stop? | Is it warm enough?
a : When the light goes. | Usually.

scene weather_limp
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #knee# knows #rain# before the #window# shows it. | The old #limp# comes back on wet days.
b : Does it stop you working? | Does it ease?
a : I slow down. | In dry #weather#.

scene waiting_cart
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Waiting beside a loaded #cart# is worse than walking with it. | I want its #wheel# turning.
b : What holds it? | Would you leave without it?
a : Usually a late buyer. | Not with my #paper# aboard.

scene open_door
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #door# in sight when we eat together. | Someone always comes home with wet #boots#.
b : Do you save a place? | Do they mind?
a : One extra #plate#. | No one has complained.

story first_vat [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : My first #sheet# came off the #frame# with a hole through it.
  : I had lifted one corner before the #water# had drained.
  ask : Did you try again?
  b : That sounds frustrating.
  : I put the #pulp# back and made another.

story long_cart [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : We carried a dry #stack# to the #city# under a canvas cover.
  : Deep #mud# held the #wheel# while a buyer waited at the far end.
  ask : Was the paper damaged?
  b : A hard journey for paper.
  : Only the cover; the #sheets# stayed dry.

story seat_by_door [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : Someone once moved my usual #seat# away from the #door#.
  : I spent the whole #meal# turning to see who entered.
  ask : Did you move it back?
  b : It is a familiar habit.
  : Before the next supper.

rule @bark_vat
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the #frame# level. | This #pulp# needs another stir.

rule @bark_door
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Leave that #door# clear. | The #road# shows through this #window#.

rule @bark_cart
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Cover the #paper# before the #rain#. | The #wheel# has found more #mud#.

rule @bark_supper
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say One more #plate# at the #table#. | The #eel# is for sharing.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #vat# is nearly ready. | #greet#. Take the #seat# facing me.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #cart# made it back today. | I kept a #plate# aside if you need one.
dlg @1 resident.job : I draw #paper# from the #vat# at #self.workplace#. | I sort #rags#, lift #frames#, and dry the #sheets#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must turn the #stack#. | #saying.capitalize#. Stay clear of the #mud#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why face the door? -> door
node door
say I like to see who comes home, especially when the #road# is bad.
free
choice What happens in the vat? -> vat
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node vat
say I spread #pulp# over a #frame# and let the #water# drain.
choice Back to the room. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. That #sheet# is holding together. | #greet#. The #cart# is under cover.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will check the #door# once more. | The #larder# has room for you tomorrow.
